ecipe requires $\\frac{2}{7}$ cups of lemon juice for every cup of water. Therefore, the lemonade has a ratio of $\\boxed{}$ cups of lemon juice to $\\boxed{}$ cups of water." :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite the fraction $\\frac{2}{7}$ as a ratio:\n\n$$\n2:7\n$$\n\nTherefore, the lemonade has a ratio of $2$ cups of lemon juice to $7$ cups of water."} :step/id #uuid "20690718-c9fc-54b6-816b-d86290bcf4f8" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484326}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484316 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484228 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00278cbd-218b-5c7a-8dee-57905a0ca05d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$2$ and $5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483568} {:answer/id #uuid "306d6638-b396-5a5e-9c83-fd117fb42399" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$10$ and $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483650} {:answer/id #uuid "6585f761-41c7-50e3-9258-db39330cd34c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$1$ and $11$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483761} {:answer/id #uuid "dae3b41a-f6fc-54c2-8c43-6a93e2d2eb57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$1$ and $10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484002} {:answer/id #uuid "e18a92f3-73f9-5576-9399-10cb385c1604" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$1$ and $5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484015}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484002} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c52abfe-a8bb-57fb-b1e7-872c00d6085b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484154}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "64676ed3-e9e9-5156-a574-3911821b3d41" :question/math-academy-id "q-92944" :question/problem "From left to right, what are the missing numbers in the following sentence?\n\nAnna requires $\\frac{1}{10}$ ounce of cocoa powder for every ounce of sugar to make a chocolate cake. Therefore, the cake has a ratio of $\\boxed{}$ ounce of cocoa powder to $\\boxed{}$ ounces of sugar." :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite the fraction $\\frac{1}{10}$ as a ratio:\n\n$$\n1:10\n$$\n\nTherefore, the cake has a ratio of $1$ ounce of cocoa powder to $10$ ounces of sugar."} :step/id #uuid "3bc58804-f419-5229-8f4c-2ed5c3724d64" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484310}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484326 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484232 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ecb1468-6372-55e5-9e8a-2c1fa8aa2ad0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483646} {:answer/id #uuid "5e7b0ce8-9530-5d61-96d4-0574b74fdfe5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483749} {:answer/id #uuid "760d6bd8-ec14-50fb-ab82-8c2e74383fbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483805} {:answer/id #uuid "9dc6d91d-264a-5f71-8480-71d2ab489853" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483891} {:answer/id #uuid "d8f144c8-0d43-5809-9bc2-812682e08229" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483998}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483646} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e02ca66-40fc-50dc-b8d3-e20362ff2ade" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484115}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6e29d990-90ac-50f9-be81-d4fdf354bbe5" :question/math-academy-id "q-92954" :question/problem "What is missing in the following sentence?\n\nJoanna cooks rice for lunch. According to the recipe, the ratio of cups of rice to cups of water is $2:4,$ so $\\boxed{}$ cups of rice are needed for each cup of water." :question/worked-solution "We can rewrite the ratio $2:4$ as the following fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{4}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the fraction by dividing the numerator and denominator by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{4}=\\frac{2÷2}{4÷2}=\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nThis means that $\\frac{1}{2}$ cups of rice are needed for each cup of water."} :step/id #uuid "60822d8e-b043-5841-b4a9-fa16caad25c8"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484342 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484280 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56e44c30-1084-5be2-a01c-ad2535a0461e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483726} {:answer/id #uuid "771b351c-dd76-56f5-b4b6-339322c69aa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483808} {:answer/id #uuid "ae8414db-6839-51e8-a990-fff4eccf5e80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483917} {:answer/id #uuid "c9e132a2-99a9-53b3-9d7f-841eaa7b465a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483967} {:answer/id #uuid "ec6a1468-df22-5e30-8c94-3e89caf0d05e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484033}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483808} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a2a655e-4e9e-5995-b06a-a119a03f5ad9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484142}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d691d9e9-ebc4-5231-9220-d7666a1593ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-60243" :question/problem "What is missing in the following sentence?\n\nA jar contains $7$ pounds of pinto beans and $9$ pounds of black beans, so there are $\\boxed{}$ pounds of pinto beans for each pound of black beans." :question/worked-solution "The ratio of the number of pounds of pinto beans to the number of pounds of black beans is  $7:9.$ \n\nWe can rewrite this ra